/* iOS Larger Text (Dynamic Type). WebKit only scales text that is sized from
   an -apple-system-* font, never px, and the home-screen app has no aA menu,
   so on iOS the root takes the reader's body size (17px at the default
   setting) and the text sizes above are restated against it: calc(Nrem/17)
   is exactly N px at the default and grows or shrinks with the setting.
   Gated on -webkit-touch-callout, which only iOS has, so desktop Safari,
   Chrome, Firefox and Android keep the px rules above untouched. Inputs
   never drop under 16px (iOS zooms the page on focus below that). Keep this
   list in step with any text size changed above; the terminal page has its
   own CSS and stays in px. */
